.TH "md_CONTRIBUTING" 3 "Version 0.2.0" "Baseer" \" -*- nroff -*-
.ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
md_CONTRIBUTING \- Contributing to Baseer 
.PP


.PP
Thank you for your interest in contributing to \fBBaseer\fP! This guide explains how to add new features, extend file format support, and follow project standards\&.

.PP
.PP
.SH "Understanding Baseer’s Extension System"
.PP
Baseer operates using \fBcallbacks\fP tied to \fBmagic numbers\fP\&. Each supported file format (like ELF or TAR) has a specific magic number that triggers a handler function when detected\&.

.PP
When Baseer opens a file:

.PP
.IP "1." 4
It reads the header\&.
.IP "2." 4
Matches it against entries in the \fR\fBbmagic\fP\fP array\&.
.IP "3." 4
Executes the corresponding parser callback (\fRbx_<format>\fP)\&.
.PP

.PP
Each \fRbx_<format>\fP function can apply multiple tool callbacks (like metadata, disassembler, or debugger)\&.

.PP
.PP
.SH "Adding a New File Format"
.PP
Follow these steps to add support for a new file type (e\&.g\&., PDF, PE, PNG, \&.\&.\&.):
.SS "1\&. Create a New Module"
Inside the \fRmodules/\fP directory, create a folder for your format:

.PP
.PP
.nf
modules/pdf/
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then add a new file:

.PP
.PP
.nf
modules/pdf/bx_pdf\&.c
.fi
.PP
.SS "2\&. Define the Format Callback"
Your callback should follow the same pattern as other formats (e\&.g\&., \fRbx_elf\fP):

.PP
.PP
.nf
bool bx_pdf(bparser* parser, void* arg)
{
    int argc = *((inputs*)arg)\->argc;
    char** args = ((inputs*)arg)\->args;

    for (int i = 2; i < argc; i++) {
        if (strcmp("\-m", args[i]) == 0)
            bparser_apply(parser, b_pdf_metadata, arg);
        else if (strcmp("\-c", args[i]) == 0)
            bparser_apply(parser, b_pdf_content, arg);
        else
            fprintf(stderr, "[!] Unsupported flag: %s\\n", args[i]);
    }

    return true;
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "3\&. Implement Tool Functions"
Create tool callbacks for specific operations:

.PP
.PP
.nf
bool b_pdf_metadata(bparser* parser, void* arg)
{
    printf("PDF metadata reader not implemented yet\&.\\n");
    return true;
}

bool b_pdf_content(bparser* parser, void* arg)
{
    printf("PDF content extractor not implemented yet\&.\\n");
    return true;
}
.fi
.PP
.SS "4\&. Register Your Format"
Edit the \fRmagics\fP array (usually in \fR\fBbaseer\&.c\fP\fP):

.PP
.PP
.nf
bmagic magics[] = {
    {"ELF", ELF_MAGIC, reverse_bytes(ELF_MAGIC), bx_elf, 0},
    {"TAR", TAR_MAGIC, reverse_bytes(TAR_MAGIC), bx_tar, 257},
    {"PDF", PDF_MAGIC, reverse_bytes(PDF_MAGIC), bx_pdf, 0},
    {NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0}
};
.fi
.PP
.SS "5\&. Rebuild"
.PP
.nf
make clean
make
.fi
.PP
.SS "6\&. Test Your Format"
Run Baseer with your new format:

.PP
.PP
.nf
\&./baseer sample\&.pdf \-m
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.SH "Naming Conventions"
.PP
Type  Example  Description  Format callback  \fRbx_<format>\fP  Main entry for file format  Tool callback  \fRb_<tool>\fP  Function used inside format callback  Header dump  \fRdump_<format>hdr()\fP  Function for metadata output  Debugger  \fR\fBb_debugger()\fP\fP  Core debugging tool  Decompiler  \fRb_decompiler()\fP  Decompiler module  

.PP
.PP
.SH "Code Style Guidelines"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Use \fBC99\fP standard\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Follow existing formatting and naming conventions\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Keep functions small and modular\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Always return \fRtrue\fP or \fRfalse\fP for callback success/failure\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Use \fRfprintf(stderr, …)\fP for error messages\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Keep console outputs colored using defined macros (e\&.g\&., \fRCOLOR_RED\fP, \fRCOLOR_GREEN\fP, \fRCOLOR_BLUE\fP)\&.
.PP

.PP
.PP
.SH "Tips for New Developers"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Start by reading existing implementations in \fRmodules/elf/\fP and \fRmodules/tar/\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Understand how \fR\fBbparser_apply()\fP\fP dispatches functions\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Use the \fBhashmap\fP inside \fR\fBinputs\fP\fP for sharing data between callbacks\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Test your module with small, well-known files\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
If your format requires byte-order conversion, use \fRreverse_bytes()\fP\&.
.PP

.PP
.PP
.SH "Future Contributions"
.PP
You’re encouraged to contribute:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
New format handlers (Mach-O, PDF, PNG, ZIP, etc\&.)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Additional tools (debuggers, extractors, analyzers)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Improvements to the CLI and parser
.IP "\(bu" 2
Documentation and tutorials
.PP

.PP
.PP
.SH "Thanks"
.PP
Your contributions make Baseer stronger and more flexible\&. Feel free to open issues or pull requests anytime! 
